        "original_id": "02dc9f9d-37a1-566e-83b5-64ca65d1e7d8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Symphony Splash\n- People: Tania Miller, Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky, Napoleon\n- Organizations: Victoria Symphony\n- Works: 1812 Overture\n\nFacts:\n- In 1812, Napoleon's Grande Armée invaded Russia, and Russia defended its motherland against the invasion.\n- In 1880, Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky wrote The Year 1812, a festival overture in E♭ major, Op. 49, popularly known as the 1812 Overture, to commemorate Russia's defence against Napoleon's 1812 invasion.\n- Tania Miller is the Victoria Symphony Music Director.\n- Symphony Splash is led by Victoria Symphony Music Director Tania Miller.",
